{{- /*
    titles.tmpl ~ Titles and naming guide template.
*/ -}}
{{- define "content" }}
<div class="row g-4 align-items-start mt-1 mb-5">
  <aside class="col-lg-3 d-none d-lg-block">
    <nav class="index-chapter-nav" aria-label="Naming guide sections">
      <div class="index-eyebrow mb-2">Sections</div>
      <ul class="nav flex-column gap-1">
        <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link index-chapter-link" href="#policy">Policy</a></li>
        <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link index-chapter-link" href="#examples">Good vs. bad examples</a></li>
        <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link index-chapter-link" href="#copy-paste">Why not copy &amp; paste</a></li>
        <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link index-chapter-link" href="#naming-rules">Naming rules</a></li>
        <li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link index-chapter-link" href="#avoid">What to avoid</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </aside>

  <div class="col-lg-9">
    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-4">

      <article id="policy" class="changelog-entry p-4">
        <div class="index-chapter-era font-monospace mb-1">Overview</div>
        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-3">Title policy</h2>
        <div class="index-prose">
          <p class="lead fs-6 fw-normal">
            Titles are important, and <em>bad titles make it hard to dupe-check uploads and search the archive</em>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-primary mb-0" role="alert">
          <strong>Keep titles simple, concise, and clean.</strong> Game titles should match the publisher's official name.
        </div>
      </article>

      <article id="examples" class="changelog-entry p-4">
        <div class="index-chapter-era font-monospace mb-1">Comparison</div>
        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-3">Good vs. bad examples</h2>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table align-middle mb-0">
            <thead>
              <tr class="small text-uppercase text-body-secondary">
                <th scope="col" class="w-50">
                  <span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center gap-1 text-danger">
                    <svg class="bi flex-shrink-0" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
                      <use xlink:href="/svg/bootstrap-icons.svg#x"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span>Avoid</span>
                  </span>
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="w-50">
                  <span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center gap-1 text-success">
                    <svg class="bi flex-shrink-0" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
                      <use xlink:href="/svg/bootstrap-icons.svg#check2"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span>Use</span>
                  </span>
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="small">
              <tr>
                <td class="text-body-secondary">Microsoft Visual Studio for WinNT V1.1001.1</td>
                <td class="fw-semibold">Visual Studio v1.1</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-body-secondary">INC cracktro for EA's Sim City 2000!</td>
                <td class="fw-semibold">SimCity 2000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-body-secondary">Zool 2 by Virgin Interactive +16 MEGA trainer</td>
                <td class="fw-semibold">Zool 2</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-body-secondary">Microsoft Windows 95 4.00.950 *STORE RELEASE FINAL*</td>
                <td class="fw-semibold">Windows 95</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-body-secondary">EA NFL 98 100% BYTE PATCHED AND WORKING</td>
                <td class="fw-semibold">NFL 98 fix</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article id="copy-paste" class="changelog-entry p-4">
        <div class="index-chapter-era font-monospace mb-1">Common pitfalls</div>
        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-2">Why not copy and paste?</h2>
        <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-3">
          Why not copy and paste from the NFO, <code>file_id.diz</code>, or the directory path?
        </p>
        <div class="index-prose">
          <p>
            It is common for Scene releases to use mismatched details, bad spellings, and lazy acronyms.
            These make it difficult to run searches for software and game names.
          </p>
          <p>
            For example, this <a href="/f/aa1d41e">release</a> for <em>The Adventures of Tintin: Prisoners of the Sun</em>
            uses <em>TINTIN (c) INFOGRAMES</em> for the DIZ, and the wrong title <em>Spirou (c) Infogrames</em> for the NFO.
          </p>
          <p>
            This <a href="/f/ae273de">release</a> for a <q>Jack&nbsp;Nicklaus 4</q> addon uses the meaningless <em><mark>JNG</mark> 4</em> in the DIZ,
            and has multiple typos in the NFO: <em>Jack <mark>Nick<u>a</u>laus <s>Golf</s></mark> 4</em>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article id="naming-rules" class="changelog-entry p-4">
        <div class="index-chapter-era font-monospace mb-1">Guidelines</div>
        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-3">Naming rules</h2>
        <ol class="list-unstyled mb-0 d-flex flex-column gap-3">
          <li class="pb-3 border-bottom">
            <div class="fw-medium mb-1">List the name of the game or software before any minimal supplementary info.</div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary">
              Examples: <mark>SimCity</mark> fix, <mark>SimCity</mark> addon
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="pb-3 border-bottom">
            <div class="fw-medium mb-1">Leave the title empty if the other metadata or screenshots already provide enough context.</div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary">
              Art, logos, courier group NFOs, and BBS/FTP adverts often do not need a title.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="pb-3 border-bottom">
            <div class="fw-medium mb-1">Do not include unnecessary information.</div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary">
              Skip semantic software versions, build numbers, or release justifications like <q>100% final</q>, <q>US release</q>, or <q>multilanguage</q>.
              <div class="mt-1"><s>SimCity 100% final, SimCity US release, SimCity 1.500.001</s></div>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="pb-3 border-bottom">
            <div class="fw-medium mb-1">Do not include overly specific or problematic details; append <q>fix</q> or <q>addon</q> instead.</div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary">
              Avoid terms like <q>cracked</q>, <q>patched</q>, <q>bytecrack</q>, <q>hack</q>, <q>key</q>, <q>keymaker</q>, <q>generator</q>, or <q>serial</q>.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="pb-3 border-bottom">
            <div class="fw-medium mb-1">Do not include redundant information.</div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary">
              Avoid words such as <q>trainer</q>, <q>cheat</q>, <q>hint</q>, <q>installer</q>, <q>cracktro</q>, <q>docs</q>, <q>documentation</q>, <q>manual</q>, or repeating the group name.
              <div class="mt-1"><s>SimCity trainer, SimCity +4 cheat, SimCity installer, Manual for SimCity, SimCity by Razor</s></div>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="fw-medium mb-1">Do not include the publisher, as it can attract automated DMCA takedowns in search engines.</div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary">
              <div><s>EA SimCity, Sim City (C) Electronic Arts, SimCity by Maxis, Sega's Sonic</s></div>
              <div class="mt-1">Exceptions are made for titles using generic nouns or verbs, such as <q>Norton Backup</q> or <q>Atari Football</q>.</div>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article id="avoid" class="changelog-entry p-4">
        <div class="index-chapter-era font-monospace mb-1">Please do not use</div>
        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-3">What to avoid</h2>
        <div class="row g-3">
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-body-tertiary">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-1">Elite text</h3>
              <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2">It is hard to read and cannot be searched.</p>
              <code class="small">εLεε7 τεxτ !s ßαd</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-body-tertiary">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-1">File names</h3>
              <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2">Filenames give no context when used as titles.</p>
              <code class="small">R-SCTY2K.ZIP</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-body-tertiary">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-1">All capitalized text</h3>
              <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2">All-caps titles are harder to scan and read.</p>
              <code class="small">ALL CAPS IS ANNOYING</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-body-tertiary">
              <h3 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-1">FTP site directory names</h3>
              <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2">Hard to read and frequent DMCA bot triggers.</p>
              <code class="small text-break">using.a.copy.and.pasted.directory.name</code>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{- end}}
